----- README.md -----
# charity-prefs-eval

Elicits and aggregates how LLMs would allocate a hypothetical $1000 across charities, over N trials.

## Framing (important)

The prompt uses an **honest hypothetical**: the model is told this is a thought
experiment and that **no real money will be donated** based on its answer. We do
*not* tell the model that real funds will be disbursed. This keeps the
elicitation clean (we measure revealed preferences, not high-stakes role-play)
and keeps the tooling free of any deception. See `src/prompt.js`.

## Usage

```bash
# Offline smoke test (no API key needed)
node src/cli.js --provider mock --trials 50

# OpenAI
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-... node src/cli.js --provider openai --model gpt-4o-mini --trials 50

# Anthropic
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-... node src/cli.js --provider anthropic --model claude-sonnet-4-20250514 --trials 50
```

Options: `--provider`, `--trials`, `--model`, `--concurrency`, `--temperature`, `--out`.

## Output

Per run, written to `results/`:
- `*.trials.json` — every raw response + parsed allocation
- `*.summary.json` — aggregates by charity and cause area
- `*.summary.csv` — same, flat CSV

## Layout

- `src/prompt.js` — system/user prompts (honest framing)
- `src/providers.js` — mock / OpenAI / Anthropic backends
- `src/parse.js` — extracts the JSON allocation block from free text
- `src/aggregate.js` — rolls trials into summaries + CSV
- `src/cli.js` — arg parsing, trial loop, output

## Notes / next steps

- The mock provider is for testing the harness only.
- Charity-name dedup is light (lowercase + whitespace/punct normalize); a real
  run may want a canonical-name map.
- Cause-area dollar attribution currently splits a trial's total evenly across
  its tags — swap for per-allocation tagging if you want precision.

